 "result_text": "`Chain.from_json(chain.to_json())` now works for predicates like `is_in`. I ran a shortened version of your example (a node match plus an `e_forward` with an `is_in` edge match), and the round-tripped chain serializes to the same JSON as the original. I didn't run the repo's test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `graphistry/compute/ast.py`. When rebuilding `filter_dict`, `edge_match` and the other match dicts, it called `ASTPredicate.from_json`. That tried to construct the abstract base class instead of the specific predicate named in the JSON's `type` field.\n\nThe repo already had a dispatcher that picks the right predicate class by `type`, in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py`, but nothing used it. I imported it into `ast.py` and used it in `maybe_filter_dict_from_json`. That function is shared by node and edge matches, so this covers all the predicate types the dispatcher lists, not only `is_in`.\n\nI made no test changes and no commit.",
